# Qt UI Rules

Qt is the primary UI framework.

## General

- Use Qt Widgets (not web-based UI unless explicitly stated)
- Prefer Qt-native patterns over custom UI systems

## Layout

- Use layouts (QVBoxLayout, QHBoxLayout, etc.)
- Avoid absolute positioning
- Keep UI responsive and scalable

## Signals & Slots

- Use signals and slots properly
- Avoid tightly coupled UI logic

## Separation

- UI should not contain heavy engine logic
- Keep logic in engine systems, not UI code

## Style

- Keep UI clean and minimal
- Follow consistent spacing and hierarchy

## Restrictions

- Do not introduce ImGui or HTML UI unless explicitly requested